  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="09c1-8be1-02a3-333f" name="Ancient Egyptian (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>ANCIENT EGYPTIAN ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.4-5), the New Kingdom (XVIII-XX Dynasties), c.1570-1080 BC.
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Standard Bearer. Chariotry up to a quarter of the points; Infantry at least a quarter; Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to a quarter.
Chariot Runners: up to one unit of runners for each unit of chariots.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Chariotry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
